Patric Mueller wrote:
> 
> The problem with /oW is that everbody wishes first for blessed scrolls
> of charging or magic markers, giving you way more wishes than it
> should.

Well, an (0:1) WoW where you have to spend the first wish for charging
(or a marker) leaves you with just three easy available wishes. Is that
too many wishes? It's a completely different issue if you find tons of
such wands, too many to even have uses for; but that's rarely the case
(if you don't exploit the game by broken pudding farming or similar;
but if you do pudding farming you'll get all objects anyway and don't
need wishes in the first place).

But then there are games where you don't find some essentials and those
three wishes seem to be very few. I've experienced all those variations
in my Nethack games, and all in all I appreciate those variances between
different games. Contrary to (commonly?) expressed opinion here I'd like
to have some options if a certain game is very stingy, even with quite
ordinary objects; it happened that (instead of the "typical" ascension
kit wishes) I wished for a magic whistle, a stethoscope, a potion cursed
gain level, or unholy water, or even an ordinary key!, while at the same
time I had still worn some lousy gear that could have been replaced.

A greater problem is, IMO, if you wish for powerful artifacts; while I
don't do that there certainly are many players wishing for artifacts.
If that would be the (only) problem with wishes, to get too powerful
objects, there's also the possibility to restrict the artifact wishes
instead of the wishes altogether. While artifact wishes are an explicit
concept in Nethack (there's a conduct!) it could be adjusted for Neohack.

